[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68334,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Thymic undifferentiated carcinoma is a primary carcinoma of the thymus lacking morphological or immunohistochemical differentiation other than epithelial differentiation. This is a diagnosis of exclusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68335,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8020/3 Carcinoma, undifferentiated, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68336,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C27.0 &amp; XH1YY4 Carcinoma of thymus &amp; Carcinoma, undifferentiated, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68337,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> anaplastic carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68338,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68339,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>Undifferentiated carcinoma of the thymus is localized in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:11:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68340,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms are related to local tumour growth or metastases {22055398}. Some cases are asymptomatic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68341,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Only 2.5% of non-neuroendocrine thymic carcinomas (18 of 706) are of undifferentiated type {25524678}. The largest reported series included 7&nbsp;cases {1991250}. The patients are adults, with no sex predominance and a median age of 54&nbsp;years {15049903; 15767803; 23319214; 22055398}. One case has been reported in a 2-year-old girl {29411634}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68342,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "<p>The rare coexistence of undifferentiated carcinoma and&nbsp;thymoma {23319214} suggests a possible derivation from pre-existing more differentiated tumours.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:11:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68343,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68344,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are often infiltrative and large {22055398}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68345,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumour cells are large and polygonal, with nuclear atypia, mitotic activity, and necrosis {1991250; 23319214; 22055398}. Squamous, glandular, or sarcomatoid features should be absent. Rarely, there can be admixed bland-looking myoid cells. Tumour cells are positive for pancytokeratins {15049903; 23319214; 22055398}. Unlike in poorly differentiated thymic squamous cell carcinoma, there is no expression of CK5/6, p40/p63, or CD5 {23319214}. Expression of KIT (CD117) and PAX8 is reported in 60% and 40% of cases, respectively {16002927; 23319214; 22055398}. Malignant germ cell tumour markers (e.g. OCT3/4 and SALL4) and neuroendocrine markers are negative.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The main differential diagnoses are poorly differentiated squamous cell carcinoma, poorly differentiated neuroendocrine carcinomas (NECs), sarcomatoid carcinoma, NUT carcinoma, malignant germ cell tumours, other malignancies (e.g. melanoma, large cell lymphoma, or SMARCA4-deficient neoplasms {30451731}), invasion from a large cell or pleomorphic carcinoma of the lung, and metastatic undifferentiated carcinoma. Cases associated with prominent inflammatory reaction mimicking Castleman disease {15767803} are probably related to micronodular carcinoma with lymphoid hyperplasia {22388764}.</p>\r\n<p>When immunohistochemistry or molecular studies are not available or appropriate, the diagnosis may be rendered provisionally.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T17:17:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68346,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68347,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Immunohistochemical and/or molecular studies for NUT and <em>SMARCA4</em> genes are helpful for the exclusion of other poorly differentiated tumours {22790861; 30362654; 30451731}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68348,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Primary malignant thymic tumour showing only epithelial differentiation and not conforming to any other defined entity</li>\r\n<li>Immunohistochemistry and molecular studies required to exclude other diagnoses</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-22T17:08:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68349,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Thymic undifferentiated carcinoma should be staged according to the TNM system [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] {25396314} and, optionally, the Masaoka&ndash;Koga system {21847052}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:11:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68350,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 244,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Undifferentiated carcinoma has a poor prognosis {15049903; 15767803; 23319214; 22055398}. In the International Thymic Malignancy Interest Group (ITMIG) database, the survival and recurrence rates are similar to those for other types of thymic carcinoma {25524678}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:09:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]